                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not sure whether they are all okay to make them as errors, but I think it makes sense.\n\nOne question I'm not clear is about \"PropertyMissing\" which seems done to accumulate messages in a loop - https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/d6a9e09897b5ed8524e0d6533e6dab80d612dfdc/redfish-core/lib/ethernet.hpp#L1813"
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/parse_registries.py",
                    "line": 400,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "FWIW, I originally did this to try to not change behavior, but I do think pretty much all of these can be errors.\n\nPropertyMissing accumulating is fine, as are any of these.  You can have multiple errors in a single request."
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/parse_registries.py",
                    "line": 400,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "I made the changes so that those are now treated as errors."
                }
            ],
