            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "The change looks good, but do we know if anywhere in the code base, that would break? \nI didn't see anything in Test \nhttps://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenbmc%2Fopenbmc-test-automation+ExtendedInfo&type=issues"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I have yet to see a client that actually parses this <propname>@<extended data> format because it's kind of a pain to do.  While there's theoretically breakage:\n1. These only happen during error conditions\n2. There are clients that parse the errors array that are potentially unbroken by this change.\n3. \"correct\" clients should also be parsing the error array where this is moving, so shouldn't be broken.  Only a client that parsed for the EXACT key would be broken.\n\nTherefore, I'm ok with this, even though it's theoretically breaking.\n\nIf you're good here, I think this can merge."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't see any clients that parse.. So I think we are good."
                },
                {
